Arrival: {
	Impact: A Kessler descent hull has broken orbit. The impact rolls across the surface.
	Assessment: KES/ARSENAL live-fire assessment authorized. Survive the audit.
	Escalation: Kessler has escalated the assessment. Reclaimer units inbound.
	Complete: Assessment complete. Kessler's public bulkhead has opened.
	Hud: KESSLER LIVE-FIRE AUDIT — {0} TARGETS REMAIN
	HudElite: KESSLER ESCALATION — {0} RECLAIMERS REMAIN
}

Dialogue: {
	Quartermaster: {
		Speaker: Quartermaster Mara Venn
		VanillaChat: Your audit cleared. That makes you a contractor, not a guest. Requisitions are priced accordingly.
		RequisitionsButton: Requisitions
		BriefingButton: Briefing
		Root:
			'''
			Assessment record confirms acceptable field survival. Kessler Armaments recognizes you as
			an independent contractor with provisional surface clearance. Do not confuse clearance
			with trust.
			'''
		OptionIdentity: "[Ask] Who are you?"
		OptionAssessment: "[Challenge] You fired on me to offer me work?"
		OptionScrip: "[Ask] What is Kessler scrip worth?"
		OptionBack: "[Back] Something else."
		OptionLeave: "[Leave] End channel."
		Identity:
			'''
			Mara Venn. Quartermaster, surface reclamation detail. I count ammunition, bodies, and
			promises—in that order, because only the first two survive an audit.
			'''
		Assessment:
			'''
			We fired near you first. The distinction is the entire test. Anyone can kill a target;
			Kessler needs contractors who can read a firing solution while standing inside it.
			'''
		Scrip:
			'''
			Scrip records useful violence performed under Kessler observation. The public counter
			accepts it for controlled stock. Coins still buy supplies; clearance buys trust.
			'''
		Allied: Your contract carries Arsenal priority. That is the closest thing Kessler issues to gratitude.
		Enemy: This counter is closed to hostile assets. Leave before the turrets finish classifying you.
	}
}
